            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0359" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg287"/>

                <head>No. 134.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14, 1882</date>.
                        (Received August 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 423.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my number 417, of the 8th
                    instant, I have the honor to acquaint you that I have to-day received from Lord
                    Granville a letter, dated on the 11th instant, in which he informs me that a
                    communication had been sent by the Irish government, reporting that Patrick
                    Slattery, one of the American suspects detained under the protection of person
                    and property (Ireland) act 1881, was released on the 1st instant.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
